<title>PERU: Peru to receive $100 mln IADB education loan.</title>
<headline>Peru to receive $100 mln IADB education loan.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru this month will receive a $100 million loan from the Inter-American Development Bank (IADB) to improve the country's educational resources, government officials said Friday.</p>
<p>IADB officials informed Economy Minister Jorge Camet and Prime Minister Alberto Pandolfi of the loan in meetings earlier this week in Washington, according to the government daily El Peruano.</p>
<p>The bank is also considering extending an additional loan of $150 million to Peru, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
